<h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
<p>Tempus is a technology company advancing precision medicine through AI-powered genomic analysis and clinical data integration. Founded in 2015 by Eric Lefkofsky, Tempus has built the world's largest library of molecular and clinical data, partnering with over 7,000 physicians and 65% of US academic medical centers. The platform combines next-generation sequencing with machine learning to provide personalized cancer treatment recommendations based on each patient's unique molecular profile.</p>
<p>What sets Tempus apart is its comprehensive approach to precision oncology, integrating genomic sequencing, clinical data analytics, and real-world evidence into a unified platform. Physicians order Tempus testing through a simple process - tumor and blood samples are sequenced using validated panels covering hundreds of cancer-related genes. Advanced AI algorithms analyze the molecular data alongside clinical information, treatment histories, and outcomes from thousands of similar patients to identify targeted therapies, immunotherapies, and clinical trials matching the patient's specific cancer profile.</p>
<p>Tempus serves oncologists, cancer patients, pharmaceutical companies, and research institutions. The platform has demonstrated clinical utility in guiding treatment decisions for solid tumors and hematologic malignancies, with studies showing improved patient outcomes when therapy is selected based on molecular profiling. With CLIA-certified laboratory operations, comprehensive bioinformatics pipelines, and continuous algorithm improvements from real-world data, Tempus represents the cutting edge of AI-driven personalized cancer care.</p>
<h2 id="features">Key Features</h2>
<div class="features-grid">
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon">🧬</div><h4>Comprehensive Genomic Sequencing</h4><p>Next-generation sequencing of 500+ cancer-related genes with high depth coverage. Detects mutations, copy number alterations, fusions, and other genomic biomarkers.</p></div>
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon"><svg class="inline-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><line x1="18" x2="18" y1="20" y2="10"></line><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="20" y2="4"></line><line x1="6" x2="6" y1="20" y2="14"></line></svg></div><h4>Clinical Data Analytics</h4><p>AI-powered analysis integrating molecular data with clinical information, treatment history, and patient outcomes. Provides actionable insights for treatment planning.</p></div>
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon">💊</div><h4>Treatment Matching Algorithms</h4><p>Machine learning identifies targeted therapies and immunotherapies most likely to benefit each patient. Matches molecular profile to approved drugs and investigational agents.</p></div>
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon"><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 3v9l-6 6a3 3 0 1 0 4.24 4.24L13 16.5V3"></path><path d="M9 3h6v6"></path><path d="M11 19.5L18.5 12"></path></svg></div><h4>Clinical Trials Matching</h4><p>Automated identification of relevant clinical trials based on genomic profile and eligibility criteria. Expands treatment options beyond standard therapies.</p></div>
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon"><svg class="inline-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"></circle></svg></div><h4>Molecular Profiling Reports</h4><p>Comprehensive genomic reports with therapy recommendations, prognostic information, and biomarker status. Designed for clinical decision-making.</p></div>
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon"><svg class="inline-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="23 6 13.5 15.5 8.5 10.5 1 18"></polyline><polyline points="17 6 23 6 23 12"></polyline></svg></div><h4>Therapy Recommendations</h4><p>Evidence-based treatment suggestions ranked by likelihood of response. Includes FDA-approved options and off-label uses supported by clinical data.</p></div>
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon"><svg class="neon-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="23 18 13.5 8.5 8.5 13.5 1 6"/><polyline points="17 18 23 18 23 12"/></svg></div><h4>Outcomes Tracking Platform</h4><p>Longitudinal monitoring of treatment responses and disease progression. Real-world evidence collection to improve future recommendations.</p></div>
<div class="feature-card"><div class="feature-card-icon"><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 3v9l-6 6a3 3 0 1 0 4.24 4.24L13 16.5V3"></path><path d="M9 3h6v6"></path><path d="M11 19.5L18.5 12"></path></svg></div><h4>Research and Discovery Tools</h4><p>De-identified data access for pharmaceutical research and biomarker discovery. Supports drug development and precision oncology research.</p></div>
</div>
<h2 id="pros-cons">Pros &amp; Cons</h2>
<div class="pros-cons-grid">
<div class="pros-box"><h4><svg class="inline-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Advantages</h4><ul><li>Largest molecular and clinical database</li><li>Comprehensive genomic panels</li><li>AI-powered treatment matching</li><li>Clinical trials identification</li><li>CLIA-certified laboratory</li><li>Rapid turnaround times</li><li>Integration of real-world evidence</li><li>Supports multiple cancer types</li><li>Evidence-based recommendations</li><li>Physician network of 7000+</li></ul></div>
<div class="cons-box"><h4><svg class="inline-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg> Disadvantages</h4><ul><li>Expensive testing (though often covered by insurance)</li><li>Primarily focused on cancer</li><li>Requires tumor tissue sample</li><li>Not all mutations have actionable targets</li><li>Complexity may overwhelm some physicians</li><li>Limited pediatric oncology coverage</li><li>Insurance authorization sometimes needed</li><li>Interpretation requires oncology expertise</li></ul></div>
</div>
<h2 id="pricing">Pricing Plans</h2>
<table class="pricing-table">
<thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td class="plan-name">xT Sequencing</td><td class="price">Variable</td><td>DNA + RNA, 500+ genes</td><td>Comprehensive solid tumor profiling</td></tr>
<tr><td class="plan-name">xF Sequencing</td><td class="price">Variable</td><td>DNA, targeted genes</td><td>Focused genomic analysis</td></tr>
<tr><td class="plan-name">xR Sequencing</td><td class="price">Variable</td><td>RNA expression</td><td>Gene expression profiling</td></tr>
<tr><td class="plan-name">Insurance Billing</td><td class="price">$0 patient cost (typically)</td><td>Covered by most major insurers</td><td>Insured patients</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2 id="use-cases">Best Use Cases</h2>
<h3>Tempus Excels At:</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Advanced Cancer Treatment Planning:</strong> Identifying personalized therapy options for metastatic and treatment-resistant cancers</li>
<li><strong>Targeted Therapy Selection:</strong> Matching patients to FDA-approved targeted agents based on specific mutations</li>
<li><strong>Immunotherapy Eligibility:</strong> Determining biomarkers like PD-L1, TMB, and MSI status for immunotherapy candidacy</li>
<li><strong>Clinical Trial Enrollment:</strong> Finding relevant trials when standard options are exhausted</li>
<li><strong>Precision Oncology Programs:</strong> Supporting institutional precision medicine initiatives</li>
<li><strong>Pharmaceutical Research:</strong> Real-world evidence generation and biomarker discovery</li>
<li><strong>Multi-Cancer Profiling:</strong> Applicable across solid tumors and hematologic malignancies</li>
<li><strong>Longitudinal Monitoring:</strong> Tracking genomic evolution and treatment resistance patterns</li>
</ul>
<h3>May Not Be Ideal For:</h3>
<ul><li>Early-stage cancers with standard treatment protocols</li><li>Patients without adequate tumor tissue for sequencing</li><li>Non-oncology applications (platform is cancer-focused)</li><li>Resource-limited settings without genomic expertise</li></ul>
<h2 id="comparison">How It Compares</h2>
<h3>Tempus vs Foundation Medicine</h3>
<p>Both are leaders in cancer genomic profiling, but with different strengths. Tempus offers broader data integration with clinical outcomes and real-world evidence, while Foundation Medicine (Roche) provides deeply validated genomic testing with extensive pharmaceutical partnerships. Tempus's AI algorithms leverage a larger clinical database for treatment matching, while Foundation Medicine's FoundationOne CDx has FDA approval as a companion diagnostic for multiple drugs. Tempus may have advantages in clinical trials matching and outcomes data, while Foundation Medicine excels in regulatory validated testing for specific targeted therapies. Many cancer centers use both platforms for complementary insights.</p>
<h3>Tempus vs Standard Cancer Treatment</h3>
<p>Traditional oncology relies on cancer type, stage, and limited biomarkers to guide treatment decisions. Tempus provides comprehensive molecular profiling revealing hundreds of potential therapeutic targets and resistance mechanisms invisible to standard testing. Studies show genomic profiling identifies actionable mutations in 30-40% of patients, with 15-20% receiving treatments they wouldn't have otherwise. While not all patients benefit from genomic testing, those with rare cancers, treatment-resistant disease, or uncommon presentations often gain valuable therapeutic options. The integration of real-world outcomes data helps predict which treatments are most likely to work for each patient's specific molecular profile.</p>
<h2 id="verdict">Final Verdict</h2>
<div class="verdict-box">
<h3>Our Recommendation</h3>
<p>Tempus represents a paradigm shift in cancer care, bringing the power of precision medicine and artificial intelligence to oncology practice. For patients with advanced or treatment-resistant cancers, Tempus genomic profiling can identify personalized treatment options that significantly improve outcomes. The platform's comprehensive integration of molecular data, clinical information, and real-world evidence provides oncologists with actionable insights for therapy selection. With partnerships across 65% of US academic medical centers and usage by over 7,000 physicians, Tempus has proven clinical utility and adoption. While genomic testing adds complexity and cost to cancer care, insurance coverage by major payers makes Tempus accessible to most patients when clinically indicated. The AI-powered treatment matching and clinical trials identification are particularly valuable when standard therapies fail or for rare cancer subtypes lacking established protocols. Tempus is most beneficial for patients with metastatic disease, multiple prior treatments, rare cancers, or when molecular biomarkers could guide therapy selection. The platform's continuous learning from real-world outcomes means recommendations improve over time as more data accumulates. For oncologists practicing precision medicine, Tempus provides comprehensive genomic analysis with clinical decision support that goes beyond raw sequencing data. The CLIA-certified laboratory and validated bioinformatics pipelines ensure test quality and reliability. If you're an oncologist seeking to incorporate precision medicine into practice, or a cancer patient exploring all treatment options, Tempus offers cutting-edge genomic analysis with actionable recommendations. While not every patient will benefit from genomic testing, those who do often gain access to life-extending therapies they wouldn't have otherwise received.</p>
</div>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What types of cancer can Tempus analyze?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Tempus provides genomic testing for virtually all solid tumors including lung, breast, colorectal, prostate, ovarian, melanoma, and rare cancers. The platform also covers hematologic malignancies like leukemias and lymphomas. Different sequencing panels are optimized for specific cancer types - the xT panel covers 500+ genes for comprehensive solid tumor profiling, while specialized panels address unique requirements of blood cancers. Tempus testing is most commonly used for advanced or metastatic cancers where treatment selection could be guided by molecular findings.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How much does Tempus testing cost?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Tempus testing costs vary by panel but typically range from several thousand dollars. However, most patients pay little to nothing out-of-pocket because Tempus is covered by Medicare, Medicaid, and most major commercial insurance plans when medically necessary. Tempus handles insurance authorization and billing directly. For uninsured patients or when insurance denies coverage, Tempus offers financial assistance programs. The company works to minimize patient financial burden while ensuring access to genomic testing. Physicians should verify coverage for specific patients before ordering.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How long does it take to get Tempus results?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Tempus typically delivers genomic testing results within 7-14 days from sample receipt at the laboratory. Turnaround time depends on sample quality, test type, and whether additional analyses are needed. Rush processing may be available for urgent cases. Results are delivered through a secure online portal accessible to ordering physicians, with comprehensive reports including genomic findings, therapy recommendations, and clinical trials matches. Tempus also provides genetic counselor support to help interpret results and discuss implications with patients.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What sample is needed for Tempus testing?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Tempus requires a tumor tissue sample (typically formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded or FFPE blocks/slides from biopsy or surgery) along with a blood sample for germline comparison. The tumor sample should be recent and contain adequate tumor cellularity. Archived tissue from prior biopsies can often be used. Liquid biopsy using circulating tumor DNA from blood is available for some indications when tissue is unavailable. Tempus provides sample collection kits and detailed instructions to referring physicians. Pathology review ensures sample adequacy before processing.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Will Tempus results change my cancer treatment?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Tempus identifies actionable genomic alterations in approximately 30-40% of cancer patients tested. Of these, 15-20% receive treatment modifications based on molecular findings. The impact varies by cancer type - some malignancies like lung cancer and melanoma have many targetable mutations, while others have fewer actionable targets. Even when specific targeted therapies aren't available, genomic profiling can identify clinical trials, predict immunotherapy response, or guide treatment selection based on similar patients' outcomes. Your oncologist interprets Tempus results in context of your overall clinical situation to determine appropriate treatment.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Is Tempus data secure and private?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Tempus maintains HIPAA compliance and implements industry-standard security measures to protect patient data. Clinical and genomic information is stored securely with encryption and access controls. When data is used for research or pharmaceutical partnerships, it is de-identified to remove personal information. Patients can consent to having their de-identified data contribute to research that advances cancer treatment, or opt out if preferred. Tempus is transparent about data use and provides detailed privacy policies. The platform's security infrastructure undergoes regular third-party audits to ensure patient confidentiality.</div></div>
</article>
